.TH PACU 8 "September 2026" "Parch GNU/Linux Project 2026" "System Administration Manual"
.SH NAME
pacu, pu \- Advanced, high-performance Pacman utilities suite for Parch GNU/Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacu
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B pu
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpacu\fR (also accessible via the short alias \fBpu\fR) is a high-performance C utility suite designed specifically for \fBParch GNU/Linux\fR (and Arch Linux derivatives). Inspired by Debian/Ubuntu's \fBapt\fR/\fBapt-mark\fR and Fedora's \fBdnf\fR, it provides native \fBlibalpm\fR integrations for repository management, safe configuration editing, dependency discovery, cache pruning, mirror ranking, and system diagnostics without script interpreter overhead.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-color=\fI<auto|always|never>\fR
Control ANSI terminal colorization. Honors the \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-config=\fI<path>\fR
Specify an alternate pacman configuration file instead of \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dbpath=\fI<path>\fR
Specify an alternate database path instead of \fI/var/lib/pacman\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-root=\fI<path>\fR
Specify an alternate installation root directory.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Simulate operations without modifying the filesystem or database.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Display verbose execution details.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress informational headers and print only essential outputs.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display command-line help and subcommand catalog.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Display version and copyright information.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Repository & Sources Management
.TP
.B edit\-sources \fR[\fIPATH\fR | \fImirrorlist\fR | \fIparch-mirrors\fR | \fIchaotic-mirrorlist\fR]
Safely edits configuration and mirrorlist files in \fB$VISUAL\fR or \fB$EDITOR\fR. Staged in a temporary file with automatic \fBlibalpm\fR syntax validation before atomic replacement and automatic backup creation (\fI.bak\fR).
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacedit\fR
.TP
.B repo list
Displays all active, testing, and disabled repositories configured in \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR, their SigLevel, and included mirror sources.
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacrepo list\fR
.TP
.B repo add \fINAME\fR [\-\-server \fIURL\fR] [\-\-include \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-siglevel \fILEVEL\fR]
Appends a new repository stanza to \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR.
.TP
.B repo remove \fINAME\fR
Removes a repository block from the configuration file.
.TP
.B repo enable \fINAME\fR | repo disable \fINAME\fR
Toggles commenting on repository stanzas.
.TP
.B rank\-mirrors \fR[\fI\-f <FILE>\fR] [\fI\-o <OUTPUT>\fR] [\fI\-t <TOP_N>\fR] [\fI\-s <TIMEOUT>\fR]
Performs concurrent HTTP/HTTPS latency and throughput probes across mirrors, generating a ranked mirrorlist sorted by fastest response times.

.SS Package Management & Holding (apt-mark equivalents)
.TP
.B hold \fIPACKAGE...\fR
Locks packages from upgrade transactions by safely appending them to \fIIgnorePkg\fR in \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR.
.TP
.B unhold \fIPACKAGE...\fR
Resumes package upgrades by removing them from \fIIgnorePkg\fR.
.TP
.B show\-held
Lists all currently held and ignored packages along with their installed versions and repository availability.
.TP
.B mark \fI<as-explicit | as-dep>\fR \fIPACKAGE...\fR
Changes the installation reason of packages in the local database.
.TP
.B check\-updates \fR[\fI\-q, \-\-quiet\fR]
Synchronizes repository databases in an isolated temporary sandbox and outputs available updates without acquiring the global pacman database lock (\fIdb.lck\fR).

.SS Dependencies & Querying
.TP
.B why \fIPACKAGE\fR
Traces and prints the reverse dependency chain explaining why a package is installed, leading up to an explicitly installed top package.
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacwhy\fR
.TP
.B deptree \fR[\fI\-r, \-\-reverse\fR] [\fI\-d <DEPTH>\fR] \fIPACKAGE\fR
Visualizes forward or reverse dependencies in an indented ASCII/Unicode tree.
.TP
.B search\-file \fIPATTERN\fR
Rapidly locates which installed package owns a specific file path or binary.
.TP
.B history \fR[\fI\-n <LIMIT>\fR] [\fI\-r\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR]
Inspects transaction records in \fI/var/log/pacman.log\fR and presents colorized installation, upgrade, reinstall, and removal histories.

.SS System Diagnostics & Maintenance
.TP
.B doctor
Comprehensive health verification tool: inspects database locks, database consistency, orphan accumulation, unmerged \fI.pacnew\fR files, GPG keyring state, and disk space across critical mount points (\fI/\fR, \fI/boot\fR, \fI/var/cache/pacman/pkg\fR).
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacdoctor\fR
.TP
.B autoremove \fR[\fI\-n, \-\-dry-run\fR] [\fI\-y, \-\-yes\fR]
Calculates the full dependency orphan tree and cleans unneeded dependency packages to reclaim disk space.
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacorphans\fR, \fBpacautoremove\fR
.TP
.B cache status
Displays package cache directory path, package count, and total disk footprint.
.TP
.B cache clean \fR[\fI\-k <KEEP_COUNT>\fR] [\fI\-u, \-\-uninstalled\fR] [\fI\-n, \-\-dry-run\fR]
Purges old package tarballs while retaining the latest \fIN\fR versions (default: 2), removes uninstalled cached versions, and purges incomplete \fI.part\fR downloads.
.br
\fIAlias Shortcut:\fR \fBpacclean\fR
.TP
.B top\-sizes \fR[\fI\-n <LIMIT>\fR]
Lists all installed packages ordered by on-disk size footprint with human-readable units and percentage of total system space.
.TP
.B verify \fR[\fI\-\-all | PACKAGE...\fR]
Verifies package file integrity and detects missing files against local ALPM databases.
.TP
.B diff
Discovers unmerged \fI.pacnew\fR and \fI.pacsave\fR configuration files, providing an interactive interface to view unified diffs, launch external merge tools (\fIvimdiff\fR, \fImeld\fR), replace, or discard files.
.TP
.B keys \fI<fix | refresh | list | reset>\fR
Keyring maintenance and repair helper.
.TP
.B news \fR[\fI\-n <LIMIT>\fR]
Fetches and formats recent Parch GNU/Linux and Arch Linux distribution announcements and critical update notices.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.conf
The primary pacman package manager configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.d/
Directory containing repository mirrorlists and drop-in configurations.
.TP
.I /var/cache/pacman/pkg/
Default package cache directory.
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
The pacman transaction history log.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/db.lck
The pacman database lock file.

